      "extract_value": "This section describes the Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale (RSE), noting it is a brief 10-item measure rated on a 4-point scale with five items reverse-coded and an overall average score computed. It reports internal consistency in the present study (women: a = .86, men: a = .82). No information about sample characteristics, study count, survey method, body appreciation/BMI measures, or correlations is provided in this section.",
      "evidence_source": "Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale (RSE; Rosenberg, 1965; German translation: von Collani &amp; Herzberg, 2003)\nThe RSE is a brief, 10-item scale measuring selfworth, rated on a 4-point scale (1 = Strongly disagree, 4 = Strongly agree). Five items were reverse-coded prior to analysis, and an overall RSE score was computed by taking the average of responses to all items. The scale showed good internal consistency in the present study (women: a = .86, men: a = .82).",
